problems.description:
Pre-existing, now incomplete instead of corrupted: other author text that the port writes into the template as unmapped text. The rename silently skips it and leaves names that no longer exist, and references report zero-width locations at the start of the block or attribute. Affected:
- snippet names and parameters (snippet_block.rs formats `name_text` and `params_text` into one overwrite of `{#snippet name(params)}`);
- each-block keys (each_block.rs pushes the key text);
- `class:` and `style:` shorthand directives.
Patches 55 and 63 make these renames partial without telling the user.

problems.fix:
Projection: keep the author's text in place, as patch 66 did for generics. In handle_snippet_block_inner:
1. overwrite `block.start..name_start` with `{pad}const `;
2. keep the name;
3. overwrite `name_end..params_start` with `/*Ωignore_positionΩ*/ = {tp}(` (and the implicit-prop form likewise);
4. keep the params;
5. overwrite `params_end..body_start` with the rest.
Do the same for each keys and class/style shorthands, and check byte-identical code with the corpus probe.
Language server, until every copy is mapped: when 55 or 63 drop a rename edit, send a window/showMessage warning that N occurrences could not be placed instead of silently returning a partial rename. Drop reference and highlight locations whose source text differs from the shadow text, as 63 does for edits.

